people with weird makeup or \u201cCG eyes\u201d.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-05T20:22:50-07:00","id":1456211,"title":"","content":"My game is a spiritual successor to our long running 1e game. I've run the players through alternate versions of stories we ran in first edition, and new stories that only work in the new 2e incarnations. They are all playing 2e versions of old characters and I introduced a (loose and very narrative fiat driven) mechanism by which their characters can remember the previous time line, and then use that information to inform their decisions in the analogus senarios. This allows me to play with themes of second chances and self-reflection. Almost all the players have played their characters as at least slightly better people in this new game and we have had multiple sessions where the characters have contemplated and discussed the impact of important decisions on the paths of their lives.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6-slagheap","name":"Slagheap","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"188"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-06T03:13:56-07:00","id":1456222,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Slagheap</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1456173-\u00e6on-your-adventures-your-themes?p=1456211#post1456211\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My game is a spiritual successor to our long running 1e game. I've run the players through alternate versions of stories we ran in first edition, and new stories that only work in the new 2e incarnations. They are all playing 2e versions of old characters and I introduced a (loose and very narrative fiat driven) mechanism by which their characters can remember the previous time line, and then use that information to inform their decisions in the analogus senarios. This allows me to play with themes of second chances and self-reflection. Almost all the players have played their characters as at least slightly better people in this new game and we have had multiple sessions where the characters have contemplated and discussed the impact of important decisions on the paths of their lives.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is awesome.<br /> \ud83d\udc4f\ud83d\udc4f\ud83d\udc4f\ud83d\udc4f\ud83d\udc4f\ud83d\udc4f\ud83d\udc4f\ud83d\udc4f\ud83d\udc4f","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1001-timecrafter","name":"Timecrafter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1001_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-24T01:43:06-08:00","id":1468737,"title":"","content":"The game I'm starting is a continuation of a very long running campaign (20+ years) using Palladium. The old game ended a bit before Aeon come out and we decided we would move some characters over from Palladium to Aeon and basically remake them as starting characters to continue the story of those characters.<br /> Basically due to player actions the characters were expelled from their old dimension and end up in Aeon. No changes made to the setting of Aeon just role playing how characters with a vastly different viewpoint would react to the setting and story of the Trinity: Continuum. We have a former super soldier/spy who hates anything that even resembles alien interference in human destiny that become a Talent, a psychic descended from mutated humans in a post apocalyptic setting that becomes a Psiad, and a dragon worshiping mage that becomes a Nova. In the old game we had a overarching plot involving the struggle of Order (good of the many out weighs good of the few) and Chaos (personal power and control is all) for the fate of the universe so I'm interested to see what happens with the Hope, Sacrifice, Unity of the Continuum.<br /> <br /> We are actually running two linked games. All of the previous Palladium games took place in the dimensions located between Order and Chaos, with the new Aeon game taking place in the Order Universe and a Scion Game taking place in the Chaos Universe. We figure once both games are well established (same players for both games, just alternating campaigns) we can have some fun set piece battles between the two groups of PCs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27184-darrendalca","name":"DarrenDalca","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27184_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-24T08:23:43-08:00","id":1468760,"title":"","content":"Haven't started it yet and still putting it together overall, but working on an Aberrant game that will be a sort of Year One scenario. There won't be an Aeon society or Project Utopia. Or any major conspiracies, benevolent, sinister, or other. At least at first.<br /> <br /> The backstory will be that after major upgrades the LHC ran an experiment. But things went far more wrong than were even thought possible and the entire facility was destroyed. Following the destruction something akin to an EMP swept the planet and even a number of satellites. In some areas it just drained power but otherwise didn't do damage and in others it destroyed electrical systems and caused even more havoc. Lastly, during the first couple of weeks following, hundreds of Novas erupted before finally tapering off to more standard eruption levels. The players will be these early Novas trying to make a place for themselves in this new world.<br /> <br /> Ideally it would take place over years in world, and if the actual game goes on long enough two story elements would take place. The discovery that Novas did exist pre N Day, and discovering the Qin nearly a century earlier than the normal timeline has it","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4178-stanlemon","name":"stanlemon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-24T17:10:48-08:00","id":1468796,"title":"","content":"I've got two groups I play with - my sons and my wife+friends.<br /> <br /> My sons and I have a family night on Fridays where we watch bad horror movies and/or good or bad action movies. We also occasionally game in a similar mood, so I'm running a Talents &amp; &quot;dark star&quot; nova campaign based loosely around The Boys (comic, not TV series). What they don't know is that I'm keeping notes and we'll later play an Aberrant game in the same setting with their old characters serving as nemesis.<br /> <br /> The gaming group with my wife and friends is a touch more &quot;traditional&quot; in that we play weekly in a long running campaign currently using 5e rules in a custom Mythical Greece themed world. Our DM for that occasionally needs a break and in those breaks I run oneshots in a setting HEAVILY based on Mass Effect with characters being either Talents, Superiors (tougher/smarter aliens), or Psiads (biotics).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26905-eternl-knight","name":"Eternl Knight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26905_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}